{{Quote|Each of our worlds has been brutalized by the Syndicates.|Enfys Nest, on the Cloud-Riders including Regineer Teed|<ref name="Solo" />}}
A '''species''' of [[Sentience|sentient]] [[humanoid]] with [[Color|yellow]]-and-blue skin and a pair of protruding [[Tooth|tusks]] existed in [[the galaxy]] by the [[time]] of the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]]. [[Regineer Teed]] was a member of the [[species]] who, in [[10 BBY]], was part of the [[Cloud-Riders]] [[pirate]] gang, with the membership of the group being drawn from [[Planet|worlds]] victimized by the [[Five Crime Syndicates]]. [[9 ABY|Nineteen years]] later, several members of the same species were also present in various [[Outer Rim Territories]] locations.

==Biology and appearance==
A [[humanoid]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]]<ref name="Solo" /> had two [[Limb|legs]] and two arms with a five-fingered hand each. It had [[Color|yellow]]-colored skin with blue stripe-like mottling. The species' head had two black [[eye]]s, no visible [[Nose|nostrils]], and a [[mouth]] with two protruding [[Tooth|tusks]].<ref name="CT" />

==Regineer Teed's species in the galaxy==
[[File:RegineerTeed-Solo.png|thumb|left|240px|Regineer Teed (background) was a member of the Cloud-Riders pirate gang.]]
[[Regineer Teed]]<ref name="CT" /> was a member of the species who was active during the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]]. They were a part of the [[Cloud-Riders]], a multi-species group of [[pirate]]s who were [[Campaigns of the Cloud-Riders|led]] by the [[human]] [[Enfys Nest]] and each of whom [[Homeworld|hailed]] from a [[Planet|world]] that had fallen victim to the depredations of the [[Five Crime Syndicates]].<ref name="Solo" /> In [[10 BBY]],<ref name="10 BBY">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'' featuring the appearance of [[Regineer Teed]] to [[10 BBY]].</ref> Teed and the other Cloud-Riders arrived on<ref name="Solo" /> the [[Outer Rim Territories]] planet<ref name="SoloGuide">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]''</ref> [[Savareen]]. There, they confronted the human [[thief]] [[Tobias Beckett]] and his [[Beckett's gang|partners]] in order to make them turn over a shipment of valuable [[coaxium]] [[Fuel|hyperfuel]], which the Cloud-Riders intended to use to finance [[Early rebellion against the Galactic Empire|resistance]] against the Empire. During the confrontation, Teed and the other pirates stood guard at the [[Bis Refinery|fuel refinery]] where Nest pled their case to Beckett's gang, with all of the Cloud-Riders at one point removing their [[helmet]]s and masks to further emphasize their leader's points.<ref name="Solo" />

[[File:RegineerTeedSpecies-TheMarshal.jpg|thumb|right|300px|A member of the species watched a gladiator fight at the Carnita arena in 9 ABY.]]
Later, the Cloud-Riders prepared an [[Showdown on Savareen|ambush]] for the [[Hylobon Enforcers|enforcers]] of the [[Crimson Dawn]] syndicate who were traveling to Savareen to retrieve the coaxium from Beckett. The pirates disguised several of the allied [[Savarian]] human locals as themselves&mdash;with one masked individual standing in for Teed&mdash;while the Cloud-Riders concealed themselves. The ruse allowed the marauders to subsequently overpower the syndicate forces, and ultimately, the gang secured the hyperfuel for themselves.<ref name="Solo" /> In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="9 ABY">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of "[[Chapter 9: The Marshal]]," "[[Chapter 11: The Heiress]]," and "[[Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine]]" to [[9 ABY]].</ref> members of Teed's species were present among the cheering spectators of an underground [[gladiator]] fight in<ref name="Chapter9">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 9: The Marshal}}</ref> the [[Gor Koresh's Honky Tonk|Carnita arena]] on the Outer Rim planet<ref name="ArtMandoS2">[[The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian (Season Two)|''The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian'' Season Two]]</ref> [[RTK111]];<ref name="SWE">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> on a [[Ocean|sea]]-port dock on [[Trask]],<ref name="Chapter11">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 11: The Heiress}}</ref> a [[moon]] in<ref name="Chapter10">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 10: The Passenger}}</ref> the Outer Rim's [[Arkanis sector]];<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> and in the [[Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary]] [[cantina]] in the [[Mos Espa]] [[City|settlement]] on<ref name="Chapter2">{{BOBF|Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine}}</ref> the Arkanis [[sector]] planet<ref name="USWNE" /> [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Chapter2" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|As the script developed, it became as they were in the end, all different races or species representing their homeworlds that had been mistreated by the Empire.|Jake Lunt Davies|<ref name="InsideTheDesigns">{{SW|url=news/solo-a-star-wars-story-designs|text=Inside the Designs of ''Solo: A Star Wars Story''}}</ref>}}
The species of which the character Regineer Teed was a member<ref name="Solo" /> was originally created by [[Jake Lunt Davies]] for<ref name="Instagram">{{Instagram|username=jakeluntdavies|url=archivefile3=File:JakeLuntDavies-RegineerTeedSpeciesTFAConcept-IG.png|name=[[Jake Lunt Davies]]|date=2023-02-11|quote=Creature concept for The Last Jedi. I originally drew him as part of an alien crowd concept sketch for The Force Awakens (featuring an early BB8 idea) and thought I’d give him another try for TLJ. He did get made for that but I don’t remember if he ever showed up in the movie.|archiveurl=https://archive.md/c1dyA|archivefile=File:JakeLuntDavies-RegineerTeedSpeciesTLJConcept-IG.png}}</ref> the [[2015]] [[sequel trilogy]] film<ref name="YearByYear">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. In a piece of concept art, a member of the species wearing a helmet was depicted [[smoking]] while leaning against a wall on a crowded street. The illustration of the [[alien]] was subsequently reworked for<ref name="Instagram" /> the [[2017]] sequel to ''The Force Awakens'', [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']],<ref name="YearByYear" /> and the character was also realized physically during the production process of that film.<ref name="Instagram" />

[[File:BeckettTeedSolo-SoloTrailerLEGO.png|thumb|right|300px|Regineer Teed (center) in a LEGO-style ''Solo: A Star Wars Story'' trailer]]
The species' first appearance, however, came in the form of Regineer Teed in the ''[[Star Wars Anthology Series]]'' film ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'',<ref name="Solo" /> which released on [[May 25]], [[2018]]<ref name="YearByYear" /> and in which the character was portrayed by [[Dee Tails]].<ref name="Tweet">{{Twitter|deetails|status/1018874896699609090|[[Dee Tails]]|quote=Yeah, Regineer Teed, is me.|archivedate=20181030063907}}</ref> The first full image of Teed was published on [[StarWars.com]] on [[February 10]], 2018,<ref name="SWcomPhotos">{{SW|url=news/new-solo-a-star-wars-story-photos-and-details-revealed|text=New ''Solo: A Star Wars Story'' Photos and Details Revealed}}</ref> with a cropped version of the same photo in which only the character's arm was visible being included in<ref name="EW">{{BookCite|author=[[Wikipedia:Anthony Breznican|Breznican, Anthony]]|container=Some people call him the... Space Cowboy|title=[[Entertainment Weekly Books|Entertainment Weekly]]|number=No. 1502|publisher=[[Wikipedia:Dotdash Meredith|Dotdash Meredith]]|date=2018-02-16}}</ref> the [[February 9]], 2018 issue of<ref name="EWcom">{{WebCite|url=https://ew.com/movies/2018/02/07/solo-star-wars-story-ew-cover|text=Venture into ''Solo: A Star Wars Story'': This week's cover|author=[[Wikipedia:Anthony Breznican|Anthony Breznican]]|date=2018-02-07|work=[[Entertainment Weekly Books|Entertainment Weekly]]|quote=To read more on ''Solo: A Star Wars Story'', pick up the new issue of Entertainment Weekly on stands Friday, or buy it here now.|archivedate=20240116183959}}</ref> the [[Entertainment Weekly Books|''Entertainment Weekly'']] magazine.<ref name="EW" /> On [[May 19]], 2018, Teed was also featured in a trailer for ''Solo'' made of [[LEGO]] parts that was released on the official ''[[Star Wars]]'' [https://www.youtube.com/c/StarWars YouTube channel].<ref name="LEGO">{{SWYouTube|qWG-4sMwW3g|Solo: A Star Wars Story Official Trailer (As Told with LEGO Bricks)}}</ref>

